{title: Pursue Peace}
{subtitle: Hebrews 12:14}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bbmaj7] | [Eb/Bb] [Bb] | [Bbmaj7] |
| [Eb/Bb] [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb/Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]All discipline seems pain[Eb/Bb]ful [Bb]
Rather than pleasant at the [Eb/Bb]time
But [Cm]later it yields [Bb]a har[Fsus4]vest
[F]Of right[Bb]eousness and peace for [Eb]us
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Pur[Gm]sue peace with everyone
[F]And holiness without [Bb]which no one will [Eb]see the [Cm7]Lord
Pursue peace with [F]everyone
[Bb]And holiness to see the face of God
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Therefore strengthen your drooping [F]hands
[Bb]And your weak knees on [Eb]the ground
[Cm7]Make straight paths for your [F]feet
So that [Bb]what is lame may [Eb]be [Gm]healed
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Pursue peace with everyone
[F]And holiness with[Bb]out which no one [Eb]will see [Cm7]the Lord
Pursue peace [F]with every[Bb]one
[Gm]And holiness to see the face [Eb]of God
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
See to it no [Bb]one falls short
Of the grace of God [F]in our lives
No bitter root [Gm]grows up
To cause trouble and defi[Eb]le many
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
No one is sexu[Bb]ally immoral
Or god[F]less like Esau did
Who sold his birthright
[Bb]For a single meal [Eb]of food
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Gm]Pursue peace with everyone
And [F]holiness without which [Bb]no one will see the [Eb]Lord
Pur[Cm7]sue peace with every[F]one
And holiness [Bb]to see [Eb]the face of God
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[F]He found no chance [Gm]to [Eb]repent
[F]Though he sought it [Bb]with [Bbmaj7]tears [Eb/Bb][Bb]
{end_of_verse}
